# Godot Project Structure

- Keep framework code separate from game code. `zfoo/` is framework-only.
- Put runnable and instanced scenes in `scene/`; put game scripts in `script/`.
- Store images in `image/`, audio in `audio/`, shaders in `shader/`, and extra binary assets in `assets/`.
- Use explicit GDScript function signatures and return types.
- Prefer `:=` for local variables when the inferred type is clear.
- Use `_ready`, `_process`, and other underscore names for engine callbacks; do not prefix ordinary business methods with `_`.
- Connect signals to readable handlers such as `on_buy_pressed` or `handle_close`.
